          dealing: "Dealer deals 3 cards to each player, one at a time, and 3 cards face-up to the table (the 'widow'). Remaining cards form the stock.",
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Have a hand with a total value closer to 31 than your opponents in a single suit.',
          gameplay: "1. On your turn, you may:\n   a) Exchange one card from your hand with one card from the widow.\n   b) Exchange your entire hand for all three cards in the widow.\n   c) Knock, if you believe your hand is high enough to win.\n2. When a player knocks, every other player gets one final turn.\n3. SCORING: Total up cards of the same suit. Ace=11, K/Q/J=10, 2-10=face value. Three of a kind (any suit) = 30.5 points.\n4. LIVES: The player with the lowest score loses one life. At zero lives, they are 'on the bus' and out if they lose again.",
          keyRules: [
            'Only cards of the same suit can be summed (except for three of a kind).',
            'Three of a kind is always exactly 30.5 points.',
            "A hand of 31 is an immediate 'Blitz', stopping the game instantly.",
            'If you knock and tie for the lowest score, you do not lose a life, but others do.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Collect high cards of a single suit. Don't hold onto low cards even if they are Aces in a different suit.",
          intermediate: "Watch the widow cards that opponents take; track which suits are being 'drained' from the shared pool.",
          advanced: 'Tactical knocking: If you have 25+ points early, knocking might catch opponents before they can assemble a viable hand.',
          tips: [
            'Aim for Aces and Face cards of the same suit.',
            'If you see a player taking many cards of one suit, avoid that suit if possible.',
            'Knocking early can be a powerful bluff.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
